First need in few words describe how we using current {{subscription}} service (let's call it Legacy Subscription) So we have {{subscription}} service, wich is a holder of all subscriptino that particular user have. This subscription have JSON details + business line. And have a calls add, getActive, redund



We use getActive subscription call on all places where we intercat with subscription on UI part



Also we have big part of subcription logic in {{rental-order-client}} service, especially logic on presenting to user wich subscription he can purchase, process of purchasing it, and if he already have some active subscription - show him how much limit he have left on it. To store this purchse history/state we have on rental_order DB {{susbcription_purchase}}, {{order_with_subscription}} tables. subscription_purchase is synced with {{subscription}} service, and basically representing the status of particular subscription in this {{subscription}} service. {{order_with_subscription}} is used to calculate usage of active subscription.

Adding management subscription_packs curently is implemented on {{rental_fleet}} service and stored on rental_fleet dd on {{subscription_pack}} table. Also we have admin endpoints on {{rental_fleet}} to show/add this subscription packs

*New logic:*

So all this purchasing/ packs management part will be replaced by new {{subscription-marketplace}} service and their client/admin endpoints. So on {{rental-order-client}} we don't need do anything regarding how user will purchase new subscriptions, he will do it over unified {{subscription-marketplace}} mechanism

Also, we don’t need this logic on {{rental_fleet}}. All packs will now be stored on {{subscription-marketplace}} service and it's schema



In terms of new logic on how we should check existing subscriptions and use it during price calculation - we have new {{subcription-benefits}} service, we will need add there new endpoint for /internal/hasRentalBeneift or smth like that, call it on order creation flow, before order creation - to show all required UI elements. Then call it at order finish during final price calculation and price breakdown creation. Then after usage of this benefit on order price - we need to send an event back to subscription-benefit service {{TypedBenefitsUsagePublisher}} {{sendUsage}} 

