*Flow Basket - Order*:

* We send a Basket Item {{name}} property as {{TranslatableField}} (it contails all available translations)
* Order saves the {{name}} as string (agnostic, good);
* On Reorder, Basket requests the “Order Basket” from Order team;
* You return the property {{name}} for every Basket Item as {{LocalisedString}}, which is only that translation that is used by the UI (user’s locale);
* We retrieve the {{LocalisedString}} and convert it to {{TranslatableField}};

You can already spot the problem. When the user places the order, we just send to the Order team the same {{LocalisedString}}, because we do not receive the {{TranslatableField}}.  At this point the Provider receives the same {{LocalisedString}}.What needs to be done:

* Order team needs to send the entire name for the basket item;

* The SP in the ticket description doesn’t have any sleeps and will cause excess load on server. I propose the following instead:

{noformat}USE taxify_customer_support;
DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS update_safety_severity_levels;

DELIMITER $$
CREATE PROCEDURE update_safety_severity_levels()
BEGIN

  DECLARE v_min_id, v_max_id BIGINT;
  DECLARE v_batch_size INT DEFAULT 2000;

  DECLARE v_sleep_cnt INT DEFAULT 0;
  DECLARE v_sleep_after INT DEFAULT 1000;
  DECLARE v_sleep_time INT DEFAULT 3;

  SELECT MIN(id), MAX(id) INTO v_min_id, v_max_id FROM taxify_customer_support.support_case;
  SELECT v_min_id, v_max_id, v_batch_size;

  WHILE v_min_id <= v_max_id DO

    UPDATE
            taxify_customer_support.support_case
        SET
            safety_severity_level = IF(is_safety_related = 1, 'minor', 'none'),
            last_update = last_update
        WHERE
            is_safety_related IS NOT NULL AND
            safety_severity_level IS NULL AND
            id >= v_min_id AND
            id < v_min_id + v_batch_size;

    SET v_min_id = v_min_id + v_batch_size;

    SET v_sleep_cnt = v_sleep_cnt + 1;
    SELECT v_min_id, v_max_id, 100*v_min_id/v_max_id AS completed, v_sleep_cnt, v_sleep_after;

    IF v_sleep_cnt > v_sleep_after THEN
      SELECT CONCAT('Sleeping ', v_sleep_time, ' sec');
      SELECT SLEEP(v_sleep_time);
      SET v_sleep_cnt = 0;
    END IF;

  END WHILE;
END;
$$
DELIMITER ;{noformat}

